        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · South &amp; Southeast Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Varanasi</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 800 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> scriptures the city, under its name Kashi, was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a>. Excavations in 2014 found artefacts dating back to 800 BCE, and two sites near the city, Aktha and Ramnagar, yielded artefacts dating back to 1800 BCE.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the left, crescent-shaped bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> in the south-eastern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, between the river's confluences with the Varuna and the Assi stream, 121 km downstream of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prayagraj">Prayagraj</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> pilgrimage, death and mourning; the ghats on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>; the Kashi Vishwanath Temple; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarnath">Sarnath</a>, where the Buddha first taught; the Bhakti poets Kabir, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ravidas">Ravidas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tulsidas">Tulsidas</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> learning and Banaras Hindu University; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> weaving</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Varanasi is a city and the headquarters of a district in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and remains a place of pilgrimage for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindus</a>, Buddhists and Jains.</span></div>
